---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/constants';
---
<BaseLayout title="About FourthWingDragon — Independent Empyrean Fan Tools" description="Meet the independent editor behind FourthWingDragon and learn about its publisher-sourced character profiles, original fan tools, and corrections policy." breadcrumbs={[{name:'About',href:'/about/'}]}>
  <h1>About FourthWingDragon</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>FourthWingDragon is an unofficial, independent English-language fan site for readers of Rebecca Yarros’s Empyrean series. It brings together short character profiles, a color and tail vocabulary index, original personality quizzes, and a fantasy name generator. Readers can explore the reference pages or choose a creative activity without opening an account.</p>
    <h2>An independent fan project</h2>
    <p>The site is maintained under the editorial pseudonym FourthWingDragon Editor. It is not owned, operated, endorsed, or sponsored by Rebecca Yarros, Entangled Publishing, or Amazon. The editor writes and organizes the site independently. Amazon shopping links are separate from the editorial work and do not make this website an official publication or a representative of any company.</p>
    <h2>What appears here</h2>
    <p>Factual character profiles are limited to public information that can be checked on the publisher’s <a href="https://www.entangledpublishing.com/books/threshing-day">Threshing Day page</a>. This includes names, the publisher’s brief descriptions, and spelling comparisons supported by that list. These profiles are deliberately short. They do not add plot summaries, character relationships, abilities, or other story details beyond that source.</p>
    <p>The quizzes and name generator are original entertainment. Their personality descriptions and invented names are creative material, not statements about the novels. The vocabulary index discusses English word formation and, where labeled, general fantasy conventions. Those explanations do not establish rules or classifications for the Empyrean series. Publisher quotations and original fan material are kept distinct.</p>
    <h2>Sources and corrections</h2>
    <p>Each factual statement should have a source link beside the relevant text so that readers can compare it with the publisher’s wording. Names and quoted descriptions are checked against that page rather than supplied from memory. If a statement cannot be verified there, it is omitted. A working link alone is not enough: the linked page must actually support the statement.</p>
    <p>Corrections follow the same standard. A useful correction identifies the affected page, the specific wording, and a publisher passage that supports the change. The editor can then compare the two and revise or remove the statement. A visible update date records an edit to a page; it does not promise a publishing schedule or imply that the publisher has reviewed this site.</p>
    {CONTACT_EMAIL && <section><h2>Contact</h2><p>For corrections, source questions, or privacy requests, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Include the page URL and relevant wording. Please do not send sensitive personal information.</p></section>}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
